[
    {
        "content": "<p>I am considering adding an instance</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNRat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but this feels too specific, so I suspect it would be hard to get accepted into Mathlib as a standalone instance.</p>\n<p>I noticed that <code>Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Nonneg.Module</code> already provides a more general construction of the form</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, this does not seem applicable to my case, because it would require something like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which is not mathematically correct: rational scalar multiplication does not preserve nonnegative reals when the scalar is negative.</p>\n<p>What I actually want seems closer to a construction of the form</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>under suitable ordered-scalar assumptions ensuring that nonnegative scalars preserve nonnegative elements.</p>\n<p>My question is: if such a general instance were added, what is the right way to make Lean synthesize</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNRat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>from it? Would this work automatically through definitional equality / existing abbreviations, or would we need additional bridge instances or equivalences between <code>NNRat</code>, <code>NNReal</code>, and the corresponding nonnegative subtypes?</p>\n<p>More broadly, what would be the Mathlib-preferred level of generality for adding this instance?</p>",
        "id": 591041186,
        "sender_full_name": "Yi.Yuan",
        "timestamp": 1777265623
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You might be interested in this recent proposal for a <code>Nonneg</code> type constructor: <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/backward.2EisDefEq.2ErespectTransparency/near/585999172\">#general &gt; backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency @ 💬</a></p>",
        "id": 591041825,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777266041
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also, this already works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNRat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 591041973,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777266135
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you for your answer. I’d like to follow up with another question.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNRat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>succeeds, but</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"bp\">≥</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"bp\">≥</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>fails.</p>\n<p>Where does this discrepancy come from?</p>\n<p>I had always assumed these were just notation-level variants, with exactly the same behavior, so this result was quite surprising to me.</p>",
        "id": 591046334,
        "sender_full_name": "Yi.Yuan",
        "timestamp": 1777269115
    },
